      "PluginCapability": {
        "description": "A single self-declared capability shown to the user for install-time\nconsent. NOT enforced at runtime (no sandbox this iteration).\n\n``capability`` is a permissive ``str`` for forward-compat: a newer\nregistry may declare a capability an older app doesn't know, and that must\nnot break parsing. The authoritative known set is enforced at build time in\nmagi-plugins ``scripts/build-registry.py`` and rendered with a known map +\ngraceful fallback in the frontend. Known values: screen_recording,\naccessibility, calendar, photos, contacts, system_media, filesystem_read,\nfilesystem_write, network, subprocess.",
        "properties": {
          "capability": {
            "title": "Capability",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "optional": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Optional",
            "type": "boolean"
